ield" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-3"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "490631e9caae6aff35de462ff8f0e18814519090b9886a5251afc49e65b0424e" "basis" 2353 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "490631e9caae6aff35de462ff8f0e18814519090b9886a5251afc49e65b0424e" "basis" 2353 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/state.json" "file_sha256" "490631e9caae6aff35de462ff8f0e18814519090b9886a5251afc49e65b0424e" "basis" 2353 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068753/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-79811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y)={x}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y)$ from $(0.5,1)$ to $(0,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =2x\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(0.5,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(0.5,1) & =2\\cdot 0.5\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{1}{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =1\\,\\text{d}x+1\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(0.5+Δx,1+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈1\\,Δx+1\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(0.5,1)$ to $(0,2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =0-0.5=-0.5, \\\\ Δy & =2-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈1\\,Δx+1\\,Δy \\\\  & ≈1\\cdot (-0.5)+1\\cdot (1) \\\\  & ≈0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y)$ increases by approximately $0.5.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79811" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34fda6fc1fa5c0d56a48f415a3f0f99075644bb87ec1abddc2d0d10cc8d89ef0"} {"question" "q-79811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.5"] ["math" "-1.5"] ["math" "0.5"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "1.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79811" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $\\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.2)$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)=\\sqrt{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y$ at the point $(4,1).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡y}{2\\sqrt{x}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{x}}{y}\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(4,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1}{2\\sqrt{4}}\\,\\text{d}x+\\frac{\\sqrt{4}}{1}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =0\\,\\text{d}x+2\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(4+Δx,1+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈0\\,Δx+2\\,Δy\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n\\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.2)=f(3.9,1.2),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(3.9,1.2).$\n\nMoving from $(4,1)$ to $(3.9,1.2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =3.9-4=-0.1, \\\\ Δy & =1.2-1=0.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈0\\cdot (-0.1)+2\\cdot (0.2) \\\\  & ≈0+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.4.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(3.9,1.2) & ≈f(4,1)+0.4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3.9}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1.2) & ≈\\sqrt{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0+0.4 \\\\  & ≈0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79841" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34fda6fc1fa5c0d56a48f415a3f0f99075644bb87ec1abddc2d0d10cc8d89ef0"} {"question" "q-79841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.35"] ["math" "0.38"] ["math" "0.40"] ["math" "0.42"] ["math" "0.43"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79841" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.40"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Estimate $(1.06)^{4.1}$ using a differential $\\text{d}f$ of the function $f(x,y)={x}^{y}$ at the point $(1,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =y{x}^{y-1}\\,\\text{d}x+{x}^{y}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(1,4),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y) & =4\\cdot {1}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{1}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{d}x+0\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(1+Δx,4+Δy),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈4\\,Δx+0\\,Δy.\n$$\n\nNote that \n\n$$\n(1.06)^{4.1}=f(1.06,4.1),\n$$\n\nso we want to move to the point $(1.06,4.1).$\n\nMoving from $(1,4)$ to $(1.06,4.1),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1.06-1=0.06, \\\\ Δy & =4.1-4=0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈4\\cdot (0.06)+0\\cdot (0.1) \\\\  & ≈0.24+0 \\\\  & ≈0.24\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis means that the value of $f$ increases by about $0.24.$ Consequently, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.06,4.1) & ≈f(1,4)+0.24 \\\\ (1.06)^{4.1} & ≈{1}^{4}+0.24 \\\\  & ≈1+0.24 \\\\  & ≈1.24\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34fda6fc1fa5c0d56a48f415a3f0f99075644bb87ec1abddc2d0d10cc8d89ef0"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1.22"] ["math" "1.24"] ["math" "1.26"] ["math" "1.28"] ["math" "1.30"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79876" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1.24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given a right cone, find the differential $\\text{d}S$ for the lateral surface area $S$ of the right cone if the base radius is $r=6,$ and the slant height is $l=10.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The  lateral surface area of the right cone is $S=\\pi rl.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(rl) & =(\\frac{∂S}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂S}{∂l})\\,\\text{d}l \\\\  & =\\pi l\\,\\text{d}r+\\pi r\\,\\text{d}l\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=6,$ and $l=10,$  the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}S(6,10) & =10\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+6\\pi \\,\\text{d}l.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79959" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34fda6fc1fa5c0d56a48f415a3f0f99075644bb87ec1abddc2d0d10cc8d89ef0"} {"question" "q-79959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "10\\,\\text{d}r+6\\,\\text{d}l"] ["math" "10\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+6\\pi \\,\\text{d}l"] ["math" "12\\,\\text{d}r+40\\,\\text{d}l"] ["math" "40\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+12\\pi \\,\\text{d}l"] ["math" "6\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+10\\pi \\,\\text{d}l"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-79959" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "10\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+6\\pi \\,\\text{d}l"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+4\\operatorname{ln}⁡({z}^{3}-y),$ use the differential $\\text{d}f$ to estimate the change $Δf$ in the value of $f(x,y,z)$ from $(2,-3,1)$ to $(1,-2,2).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(x,y,z) & =(\\frac{∂f}{∂x})\\,\\text{d}x+(\\frac{∂f}{∂y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{∂f}{∂z})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =2x\\,\\text{d}x-(\\frac{4}{{z}^{3}-y})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{12{z}^{2}}{{z}^{3}-y})\\,\\text{d}z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt the point $(2,-3,1),$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}f(2,-3,1) & =(2\\cdot 2)\\,\\text{d}x-(\\frac{4}{{1}^{3}-(-3)})\\,\\text{d}y+(\\frac{12\\cdot {1}^{2}}{{1}^{3}-(-3)})\\,\\text{d}z \\\\  & =4\\,\\text{d}x-\\,\\text{d}y+3\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, if we move to the point $(2+Δx,-3+Δy,1+Δz),$ then we can approximate the change in $f$ as\n\n$$\nΔf≈4\\,Δx-\\,Δy+3\\,Δz.\n$$\n\nMoving from $(2,-3,1)$ to $(1,-2,2),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δx & =1-2=-1, \\\\ Δy & =-2-(-3)=1 \\\\ Δz & =2-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δf & ≈4\\,Δx-1\\,Δy+3\\,Δz \\\\  & ≈4\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 1+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & ≈-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $f(x,y,z)$ decreases by approximately $-2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "34fda6fc1fa5c0d56a48f415a3f0f99075644bb87ec1abddc2d0d10cc8d89ef0"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-1"] ["math" "-2"] ["math" "-3"] ["math" "-4"] ["math" "1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"} {"question" "q-86715" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074270/state.json" "file_sha256" "9321f06fa0f700f8d67535a2811bc232478545811ec5ffda4d802d0e85cde98b"}] "usage" {"q-79811" [] "q-79876" [] "q-86715" []} "basis" 2731 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [17592186360044 17592186360045 17592186360046 17592186360047 17592186360048 17592186360051 17592186360052 17592186360053 17592186360054 17592186360055 17592186369170 17592186369171 17592186369172 17592186369173 17592186369174] "immutable_fields" [[17592186360043 :answer-field/correct] [17592186360043 :answer-field/id] [17592186360043 :answer-field/key] [17592186360043 :answer-field/type] [17592186360050 :answer-field/correct] [17592186